{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:693c559e842aadf93ddcaba5f140c97aac1419c23fda3c1038c7a690c13b1213", "sample_idx": 31, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "Section 1\nThe Guardian has issued corrections to several articles that were published recently. The corrections address various errors that were found in the articles, including mistakes in the reporting of new laws and incorrect information about individuals.\n\n*** \nSection 2\nSome of the corrections include clarifying that a new law making the abduction of a cat or dog a specific criminal offence applies to England and Northern Ireland, not the entire UK. The corrections also address errors in the reporting of individuals, including Eileen Burbidge's role at Fertifa and the family background of the characters in the film Bend It Like Beckham. Two of the corrections are: \n* The new pet theft law applies to England and Northern Ireland, not the UK as a whole.\n* Eileen Burbidge is the executive director of Fertifa, not the founder.\n\nSection 3\nThe corrections demonstrate the Guardian's commitment to accuracy and transparency in their reporting. By correcting errors and providing clarification, the Guardian aims to provide readers with the most accurate information available.\n\nSection 4\nReaders can contact the Readers' Editor to report any errors or concerns they may have. \n* The Readers' Editor can be reached by email at observer.readers@observer.co.uk or by phone at 020 3353 4736.\nP.P.S The Guardian values the input of its readers in ensuring the accuracy of its reporting.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Section", "logprob": -2.8013790142722428e-05}, {"token": " ", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " Guardian", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": " has", "logprob": -0.1049228385090828}, {"token": " issued", "lo